# Every change is reviewed before it merges. With "require review from Code
# Owners" switched on in the ruleset for main, GitHub enforces this rather than
# relying on anyone remembering it.
#
# Both owners review ordinary work, so neither is a bottleneck on the other.
# GitHub counts a code owner only if they have write access to the repository.
# Until the second contributor has it, the catch-all names one eligible person.
# Nobody can approve their own pull request, so this still means a second pair
# of eyes on ordinary work. On the owner-only paths below there is no second
# code owner, so an owner-authored change there has no eligible reviewer.
*                         @pewpewpressco-ux @eternalaether5

# The governance records are the owner's alone. docs/OwnerDecisions.md Part 11a
# grants the second contributor no authority over them. Most of these paths are
# in AGENTS.md under "What only the owner may change"; AGENTS.md reserves only
# ADR *statuses* in docs/DECISIONS.md, and does not name AGENTS.md or .github/
# at all, so those three are this file being stricter, not quoting it.
